  <section class="flu-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">H1N1 influenza · the deadliest pandemic in modern history</span>
    <h1 class="disp">The pandemic <span class="light">that outkilled</span><br><span class="gold">the war.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">It arrived in the last year of World War I and killed more people than the war did — in about a third of the time, with no vaccine, no antiviral, and no idea yet that viruses even existed. It got its name from the one country honest enough to report it.</p>
    <div class="flu-hero-stats" aria-label="1918 influenza pandemic at a glance">
      <div><span class="n">50–100M</span><span class="k">deaths worldwide — more than WWI's battlefield deaths</span></div>
      <div><span class="n">~500M</span><span class="k">people infected — roughly a third of the world's population</span></div>
      <div><span class="n">~2.5%</span><span class="k">case-fatality rate — twenty-five times a typical flu</span></div>
      <div><span class="n">1918</span><span class="k">year its deadliest wave began, mid-war</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

